{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>Then he arose and went and Esau despised, etc.</b> Meaning: the Torah testifies about him that he despised the birthright in his own mind. Therefore it did not suffice to say ״וַיִּבֶז״ (and he despised) and return to Esau mentioned just above — understand this. And the intent of this declaration is to say that even without the reason stated earlier, he was fully resolved, for in his eyes it was a contemptible thing, and he would sell it for something — even though he had no need to recover himself and was fully resolved and conveying ownership."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:43:24.456989522Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}